From efed5e3816c4f4c50f20d58f08da20e82594b907 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 14:38:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] media: platform: add the HiSTB H.264 encoder driver

The VEDU encoder family of the HiSTB set-top-box SoCs has no mainline
driver.

The v2 block of hi3716cv200 and hi3798mv100 is programmed through
register writes and a 64-byte packet ring, codes IDR and P pictures, and
its device-tree match belongs to one platform driver so a later
generation can attach as a second backend. Add the shared core and the
v2 backend.

Signed-off-by: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
